// Specialised: claims, unrest and rebellion.

:: anchor=left size=20 pad=26 enter=type speed=44 line=1.4

@Signals Officer
:: point=tab.claims gate=1 until=open:claims
Claims and unrest. Open the claims panel. These are one subject, whatever the interface says.
---
@Signals Officer
A §**claim**§ is the difference between a war the world tolerates and a war
that unites everyone against you. Press one you hold and you are settling a
grievance; take ground you never claimed and you are the grievance.
---
@Signals Officer
Make the claim §**before**§ the war, not after. A claim filed the turn after
you took the province fools nobody and costs the same.
---
@Signals Officer
:: point=panel.close gate=1 until=closed:claims
Close it.
---
@Signals Officer
§**Unrest**§ is what taking ground does to the ground. Conquered provinces
resent it, minorities resent it more, and conscription and censorship both
buy you strength now against unrest later.
---
@Signals Officer
Past a threshold a province stops paying and starts organising. Past the next
one it leaves -- and it leaves as a §**country**§, with your industry, your
population and a very specific opinion of you.

You get a warning. You do not always get a second one.
---
@Signals Officer
The cures are unpopular or slow: garrison it, spend on it, or give it what it
wants. Choose early, because all three take turns to work.

That is unrest. Anything else?
